        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://purl.oboInOwllibrary.org/oboInOwl/NCIT_C66830"/>
        <rdfs:label>Extrapyramidal Symptom Rating Scale-Abbreviated Clinical Classification</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCIT_C118457 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCIT_C118457">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IDOMAL_0000373"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A protein complex that plays a role in both NMDA binding and ion transport. It is a heterotetramer consisting of 2 glutamate [NMDA] receptor subunit zeta-1 proteins and 2 epsilon subunits (glutamate [NMDA] receptor subunit epsilon-1, -2, -3 or -4).</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000412 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ncit.owl"/>
        <obo:NCIT_NHC0>C118457</obo:NCIT_NHC0>
        <obo:NCIT_P106>Amino Acid, Peptide, or Protein</obo:NCIT_P106>
        <obo:NCIT_P108>N-Methyl-D-Aspartate Receptor</obo:NCIT_P108>
        <obo:NCIT_P207>C0080093</obo:NCIT_P207>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>N-Methyl-D-Aspartate Receptor</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>N-Methyl-D-aspartate receptor</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>NMDA Receptor</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>NMDAR</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <rdfs:label>N-Methyl-D-Aspartate Receptor</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCIT_C118892 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCIT_C118892">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCIT_C20130"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A subfamily within the forkhead box (FOX) protein family, which is a family of transcription factors that contain a forkhead DNA-binding domain. FOXO proteins regulate apoptosis, cell-cycle progression, oxidative-stress resistance, and tumor suppression. The transcriptional promoter activity of these factors is regulated by post-translational modifications, such as phosphorylation, acetylation, and monoubiquitination.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000412 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ncit.owl"/>
        <obo:NCIT_NHC0>C118892</obo:NCIT_NHC0>
        <obo:NCIT_P106>Amino Acid, Peptide, or Protein</obo:NCIT_P106>
        <obo:NCIT_P107>FOXO Family</obo:NCIT_P107>
        <obo:NCIT_P108>FOXO Family</obo:NCIT_P108>
        <obo:NCIT_P207>C3899164</obo:NCIT_P207>
        <obo:NCIT_P322>CTRP</obo:NCIT_P322>
        <obo:NCIT_P98>There are four known members of the FOXO family expressed in humans. They are FOXO1, FOXO3, FOXO4 and FOXO6.</obo:NCIT_P98>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>FOXO</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>FOXO Family</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>Fork Head Box Transcription Factor Class O</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>Forkhead Box Transcription Factor Class O</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>FoxO</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://purl.oboInOwllibrary.org/oboInOwl/NCIT_C116977"/>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://purl.oboInOwllibrary.org/oboInOwl/NCIT_C142799"/>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://purl.oboInOwllibrary.org/oboInOwl/NCIT_C142800"/>
        <rdfs:label>FOXO Family</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCIT_C1192 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCIT_C1192">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_25710"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_33304"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A phospholipid that is a component of the plasma membrane with signal transduction inducing activity. Phosphatidylinositol 4,5-bisphosphate (PIP2) is an intermediate that can be converted into either the second messenger signaling molecules, inositol 1,4,5-trisphosphate (IP3) and diacylglycerol (DAG), or phosphatidylinositol (3,4,5)-trisphosphate (PtdIns(3,4,5)P3; PIP3). Both PIP2 and PIP3 can act as docking phospholipids, which recruit signaling proteins to the plasma membrane and promotes the activation of several signaling cascades.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000412 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ncit.owl"/>
        <obo:NCIT_NHC0>C1192</obo:NCIT_NHC0>
        <obo:NCIT_P106>Biologically Active Substance</obo:NCIT_P106>
        <obo:NCIT_P106>Organic Chemical</obo:NCIT_P106>
        <obo:NCIT_P108>Phosphatidylinositol 4,5-bisphosphate</obo:NCIT_P108>
        <obo:NCIT_P207>C0070798</obo:NCIT_P207>
        <obo:NCIT_P366>Phosphatidylinositol_4_5-bisphosphate</obo:NCIT_P366>
        <obo:NCIT_P368>CHEBI:18348</obo:NCIT_P368>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>1,2-Diacyl-sn-Glycero-3-Phospho-(1&apos;-myo-Inositol-4&apos;,5&apos;-Bisphosphate)</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>1-O-(3-sn-Phosphatidyl)-1D-myo-Inositol 4,5-Bis(Dihydrogen Phosphate)</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>1-Phosphatidyl-1D-myo-Inositol 4,5-Bisphosphate</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>1-Phosphatidyl-D-myo-Inositol 4,5-Bisphosphate</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>PIP2</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>PIPP</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>Phosphatidyl-myo-Inositol 4,5-Bisphosphate</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>Phosphatidylinositol 4,5-Diphosphate</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>Phosphatidylinositol 4,5-bisphosphate</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>PtdIns(4,5)P2</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>PtsIns-4,5-P2</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <rdfs:label>Phosphatidylinositol 4,5-bisphosphate</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCIT_C120257 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCIT_C120257">
