        <obo:NCIT_P322>CTRP</obo:NCIT_P322>
        <obo:NCIT_P325>A noninvasive tool used to observe functioning in the brain or other organs by detecting changes in chemical composition, blood flow, or both.</obo:NCIT_P325>
        <obo:NCIT_P325>A type of MRI that takes a series of images of an organ in quick succession and statistically analyzes the differences between the images.</obo:NCIT_P325>
