        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0000062"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Anatomical structure that has as its parts two or more multi-tissue structures of at least two different types and which through specific morphogenetic processes forms a single distinct structural unit demarcated by bona fide boundaries from other distinct anatomical structures of different types.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000232>this class was introduced for consistency with CARO. However, in this ontology we typically classify organs directly under &apos;organ&apos; rather than subdividing into compound and simple organs</obo:IAO_0000232>
